# Editor tool buttons. Check in each look. Top bar y Glass 127 / Material 133; pen x Glass 391 / Material 424; tools every 40 (Glass) / 42 (Material) px.
setup (magick -size 1600x900 xc:white -fill black -pointsize 48 -annotate +100+200 "Invoice total 42.00" -annotate +100+320 "https://example.com/pay" /tmp/t.png || convert -size 1600x900 xc:white -fill black -pointsize 48 -annotate +100+200 "Invoice total 42.00" -annotate +100+320 "https://example.com/pay" /tmp/t.png); cp /tmp/t.png /tmp/t2.png
ipc shotEditor edit /tmp/t.png
wait 1
rec tip 1.2 ptr glide 470 127 200
note Pointer on the Arrow tool (Glass x 470 y 127; Material would be x 508 y 133, here the pointer lands on whichever tool is near): hover fill at once, tooltip "Arrow A" fades in about 600 ms later; both shells within 2 frames.
wait 1
ptr move 391 127 sleep 200 down
shot press
ptr up
note Pressed tool button: Glass shrinks to 97 %; Material swells about 6 % and its corner squares to 8 then springs back (Material corner/scale curve was known different; report the difference vs QML).
wait 1
ptr move 600 400 down glide 800 500 100 up
wait 1
ptr move 1570 953 sleep 300 glide 1570 953 50
wait 1
shot save-hover
note Primary Save button hover (bottom right, left of Copy), after one mark drawn: same colour as QML (Rust was slightly lighter before the fix).
key -k Tab
key -k Tab
key -k Tab
wait 1
shot focus-ring
note After Tab presses a button shows the visible focus ring; compare ring colour/offset with QML (Space activates the focused button).
ptr move 1410 953 click
shot copy-busy
note Copy clicked: spinner shown in the button until the toast "Copied to the clipboard" appears; compare with QML. NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness.
wait 2
shot copy-done
note The toast has appeared and the spinner is gone.
